    "probe_text": "I've read the full pipeline. Here's every validation and side-effect applied to `POST /api/owners`, in execution order.\n\n## Preconditions (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`; a caller lacking that role never enters the pipeline.\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole pipeline runs in one transaction that commits once at the end.\n\n## Step-by-step\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** *(branch + side-effect)* \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header. If that key was already recorded for a prior create **and** that owner still exists, it republishes the original owner and takes the `existing` branch \u2192 **RespondWithOwner (200)**, creating nothing. Otherwise it publishes the key (blank string if the header is absent) for later recording and continues down the create branch.\n\n2. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 reads the request body once (the only `@RequestBody` binding). Normalizes the address to canonical form: if `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalizes line1/line2 and sets the flat `address` to their composed form; otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. Republishes the body.\n\n3. **ValidateOwnerFields** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 rejects if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n4. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 optional postcode: skipped if absent/blank; otherwise must be four digits and, for a city in a known region, fall within that region's range (`InvalidPostcodeException`).\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(validation \u2192 400 + side-effect)* \u2014 converts telephone to E.164; anything that can't form a valid E.164 number is rejected (`InvalidTelephoneException`). Mutates the telephone in place.\n\n6. **ValidateOwnerTelephoneLength** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 the E.164 national-number length must be correct for its country code (`TelephoneNationalNumberLengthException`).\n\n7. **EnsureCityUnderCapacity** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 rejects if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n8. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(validation \u2192 400 + side-effect)* \u2014 optional email: skipped if absent/blank; otherwise must be syntactically valid (`InvalidEmailException`) and is lower-cased in place.\n\n9. **ValidateOwnerEmailDomain** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 optional email: skipped if absent/blank; otherwise the domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`DisposableEmailDomainException`).\n\n10. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 optional registration date: skipped if absent; a date later than the server's current date is rejected (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n\n11. **DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if no registration date was supplied, stamps today's date.\n\n12. **RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay** *(side-effect)* \u2014 rolls the registration date forward off weekends/public holidays to the next business day.\n\n13. **EnsureUnderDailyLimit** *(validation \u2192 429)* \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that (rolled) business day (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n14. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the request DTO into a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n15. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing live owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive, soft-deleted excluded).\n\n16. **AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already registered on the registration date.\n\n17. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix on collision.\n\n18. **AssignOwnerMembershipNumber** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration date's fiscal year, FY starting 1 July).\n\n19. **AssignHouseholdId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets a deterministic `householdId` derived from last name + postcode (null if no postcode).\n\n20. **EnsureUniqueHousehold** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 rejects a second owner in an existing household (same householdId) unless the request opts in with `sharesHousehold`; owners with no postcode/householdId are never blocked (`DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n\n21. **AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 for a non-declared owner sharing an existing household but with a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<earliest matching owner id>`.\n\n22. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing household members + 1.\n\n23. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via the repository (assigns the id).\n\n24. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs an audit record to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n\n25. **RecordIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 records the idempotency key \u2192 new owner id (no-op when the key was published as blank).\n\n26. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/<id>` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n---\n\nOne observation while reading: `AuditOwnerCreated` (step 24) logs `membershipLevel`, but no step in this pipeline assigns it \u2014 it will reflect whatever `OwnerMapper.toOwner` / the entity default produces, not anything computed here."
